Error [jet.InvalidAuthorityBlock]: The package's `authority:` block is malformed
  --> tests/ui/ffi_library_grant_names_its_language.jet:6:5
    |
  6 |     authority: { allow: [FFI("c"), IO, Mem.Alloc] }
    |     ^^^^^^^^^
 Why: `FFI("c")` names the library `c` without its language; a library belongs to one language, so write `FFI.C("c")` for a C library
 Fix: `authority:` declares `allow`, `deny`, `needs`, `grants`, `trust`, and `providers` using canonical rights
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E1221
